Considering the arguments advanced by both the parties and overall circumstances of the case, but without commenting on merits of the case, this Court is inclined to grant anticipatory bail to the applicant.
Thus, the application is allowed.
Accordingly, it is directed that in the event of arrest of applicant, applicant- SHIVSHANKAR RAWAT shall be released on bail in relation to Crime No.20 of 2024, registered at Police Station STF Bhopal Unit, Gwalior for offence punishable under Sections 419, 420, 468, 471, 120-B of IPC and Section 3-D/4 of Manyata Prapt Pariksha Adhiniyam, upon furnishing a personal bond in the sum of Rs.1,00,000/-(Rupees One Lakh Only) with one solvent surety of the same amount to the satisfaction of the Officer making arrest, for compliance with the following conditions: (For convenience of understanding by accused and surety, the conditions of bail are also reproduced in Hindi as under):-
(1) Applicant shall make himself available for investigation as may be directed by the officer, in-charge of investigation;
